WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.220
Batfleck has officially sent his cape and
cowl to the cleaners and flown out of Wayne

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:05.720
Manor.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.740
Speaking during his appearance on the Thursday,
February 14th episode of Jimmy Kimmel Live!,

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:15.640
Ben Affleck finally came forward and explained
in no uncertain terms why he is no longer

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.640
playing Batman.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.940
"I'm...not Batman?"

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.510
Unlike the circumstances surrounding and sequence
of events leading up to Affleck's departure

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:28.120
from the coveted comic book character role,
his actual reason for ditching the post is,

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.860
surprisingly, not complex in the slightest:
he simply couldn't craft an iteration of the

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.740
Dark Knight that he was happy with for the
forthcoming standalone film The Batman.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.920
"But I just couldn't come with with a version"
through "time to let someone take a shot at

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.420
it."

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.340
Affleck's ties to the DC Extended Universe
and to his role as Batman that he originated

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:54.000
in 2016's Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice
have been frayed for over two years now.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.360
After taking turns in Justice League and Suicide
Squad, Affleck was eyeing a sparkling new

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:04.750
project: a standalone pic entitled The Batman
that he was originally slated to write, direct,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.300
and lead.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:11.340
Announced in July of 2015, those initial grand
plans for The Batman began to fall apart when

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:15.920
Affleck backed out of his position as director,
handing the reins to War for the Planet of

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.500
the Apes filmmaker Matt Reeves after coming
to the tough realization that he didn't have

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.990
the wherewithal to work behind the camera
and act in front of it without sacrificing

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.740
quality in one of the two jobs.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.720
"A human being can only absorb so much."

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.560
Affleck said in late January of 2017:

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.719
"Performing this role demands focus, passion,
and the very best performance I can give.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.640
It has become clear that I cannot do both
jobs to the level they require.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.220
Together with the studio, I have decided to
find a partner in a director who will collaborate

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.680
with me on this massive film."

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:52.719
At the time, Warner Bros. assured that the
studio supported Affleck's decision not to

00:01:52.719 --> 00:01:57.520
direct The Batman and remained, quote, "committed
to working with him to bring a standalone

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.800
Batman picture to life."

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:04.579
Flash forward to July of 2018, when Deadline
issued a report claiming Affleck was well

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:08.580
and truly done with The Batman and wouldn't
be reprising his role again.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.640
Just a few months later, The Hollywood Reporter
published its own piece reporting that the

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.260
actor was indeed leaving the DCEU.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.280
"Something tells me we're not getting the
band back together."

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.040
This all brings us to now: a time in which
there is no actor attached to lead The Batman,

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.600
no star standing firm in the DC movie world
as Bruce Wayne.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.220
This isn't to say that Reeves has no idea
what to do with the film without Affleck in

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:36.180
tow, or that Warner Bros.' well of contenders
for the new Batman is dry.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.940
It's quite the opposite, really.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.480
Several big-name stars are reportedly in consideration
to take over for Affleck in The Batman, from

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.620
Robert Pattinson and Kit Harington to Armie
Hammer and Aaron Taylor-Johnson.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.380
"I want to team up, like Batman and Robin."

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.260
Things are looking just as bright for Reeves,
who has a clear vision for what The Batman

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:55.900
will feel like.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.860
He previously teased to The Hollywood Reporter
that he intends to cast a collection of characters

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.020
from Batman's massive rogues gallery.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:07.540
"Clock king Calendar man, Kite Man, Cat Man,
Zebra Man, and the Condiment King!

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.800
“Okay, are you making some of those up?"

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.819
"nope, they're all real."

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.830
Reeves also said that the film is heavily
inspired by film noir, saying:

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.340
"It's very much a point of view-driven, noir
Batman tale.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.440
It's told very squarely on his shoulders,
and I hope it's going to be a story that will

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.280
be thrilling but also emotional.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:29.360
It's more Batman in his detective mode than
we've seen in the films.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.400
The comics have a history of that.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.730
He's supposed to be the world's greatest detective,
and that's not necessarily been a part of

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.780
what the movies have been."

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:41.480
No matter who ends up donning the Bat-suit
next, it sounds like Affleck is in good spirits

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.560
over the situation and that Reeves is confident
in his ideas for The Batman.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:50.720
Warner Bros. has the film slated to premiere
in theaters on June 25th, 2021 - plenty of

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.780
time to select a fresh face to become the
next Batman.

